    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d509">

                <pb facs="0717" n="629" xml:id="pg629"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr. Scruggs.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-10-05"><hi rendition="#italic">October 5,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Foster states that the blockade is made effective by the presence of
                    blockading vessels competent to warn and prevent entrance, and that if blockade
                    be intermitted, commercial vessels should not be prevented from entering nor
                    protected in breaking actual blockade. He informs Mr. Scruggs that instructions
                    in this sense will be sent to naval vessels of the United States, and directs
                    him to advise steamers that they should not attempt to break the blockade when
                    it is visible.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
